## Workflow skills

Tool-agnostic procedures in `skills/`, loaded on demand:

| Skill | Trigger | Output |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `/explore` | Understand a codebase area | Relevant files, patterns, open questions |
| `/spec` | Define a feature | Requirements, acceptance criteria, edge cases, out-of-scope |
| `/plan` | Structure an implementation | Ordered steps with dependencies + verification |
| `/test` | Derive tests from spec | Pytest functions per acceptance criterion |
| `/delegate` | Hand off to an autonomous agent | Self-contained brief: spec + plan + tests + constraints |
| `/review` | Independent review of a change | Findings by severity, ship/fix-then-ship/needs-rework verdict |
| `/verify` | Prove the change works on the current diff | Fresh evidence (command + output) mapped to acceptance criteria |
| `/debug` | Find a root cause | Repro, hypotheses, root cause, fix + regression test |
| `/capture` | Save a learning | One-line dated rule with *why* |
